          "unit": "",
          "referenceRange": "Approx. 275–295 mOsm/kg",
          "lowInterpretation": [],
          "highInterpretation": [],
          "notes": [
            "Low measured osmolality with hyponatraemia confirms hypotonic hyponatraemia. Normal/high osmolality suggests glucose, mannitol or another effective osmole, or pseudohyponatraemia."
