          "unit": "",
          "referenceRange": "Usually <10 mOsm/kg, formula/laboratory dependent",
          "lowInterpretation": [],
          "highInterpretation": [],
          "notes": [
            "A raised gap can occur with toxic alcohols, ethanol, ketones, lactate, renal failure or laboratory/formula variation. A normal gap does not exclude late toxic alcohol poisoning."
